    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d338">

                <pb facs="0663" n="567" xml:id="pg567"/>

                <head>No. 336.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Watson to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Newport, R. I.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-07-30"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 30, 1874</date>.
                        (Received August 3.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to your letter of the 27th
                    instant, which I received last evening, I have the honor to inform you that I
                    telegraphed to you this morning as follows, “The boundary-line between Labrador
                    is a line drawn due north and south from the Bay or Harbor of Ance Sablon,
                    inclusive, as far as fifty-second degree of north latitude. (See Imperial
                    Statutes 6, George IV, cap. 59.) Labrador is under the jurisdiction of
                    Newfoundland.”</p>
                <p>I informed you at the same time that I should communicate to you the dispatch on
                    the subject which I expect from Lord Dufferin, so soon as I receive it.</p>
                <p>I regret much if you have been put to any inconvenience by the delay in replying
                    to your note to Sir Edward Thornton, of the 19th of June last.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>R. G. WATSON.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
